{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/930832-just-for-fun-mortal-kombat-fighting-style","id":930832,"title":"[Just For Fun] Mortal Kombat Fighting Style","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-13T07:22:09-07:00","id":930832,"title":"[Just For Fun] Mortal Kombat Fighting Style","content":"While this is mostly for comical purposes, if someone good with crunch has tips for making this playable, I'd love to hear them.<br /> <br /> <b>Mortal Kombat (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Strength \u2022\u2022\u2022, Stamina \u2022\u2022\u2022, Brawl \u2022\u2022, Weaponry \u2022\u2022, Expression or Intimidation \u2022\u2022<br /> <br /> <b>Tough As Nails (\u2022):</b> You can take a lot more punishment than you ought to. Add [your dots in this Style/2 round up] to your effective Stamina to calculate your Health and how much damage you must take to suffer a Tilt. Also, you gain 1/1 Armor, which applies against lethal damage and stacks with Merits and actual Armor.<br /> <br /> <b>Rivers Of Blood (\u2022\u2022):</b> You may reduce your opponent\u2019s effective Stamina by your [dots in Athletics, Brawl or Weaponry/2 round up] for the purposes of inflicting Tilts a number of times per scene equal to your dots in this Style. Your Brawl, Weaponry and Athletics attacks inflict lethal even on opponents that would downgrade the damage to bashing.<br /> <br /> <b>Vicious Projectile (\u2022\u2022\u2022):</b> You may spend 1 willpower point to make an Athletics, Brawl or Weaponry attack from up to [your dots in Brawl or Athletics x 5] yards away. You reduce penalties for targeted attacks by [your dots in this Style/2 round up], down to a minimum of -1.<br /> <br /> <b>X-Ray (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022):</b> When you perform a targeted attack, you gain 9 Again. If you also perform an All-Out Attack, you gain 8 Again. If you inflict more damage than the opponent\u2019s effective Stamina, you may inflict a custom Tilt.<br /> <br /> <b>FINISH HIM! (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022):</b> If your opponent has all of his Health boxes filled with lethal damage or is suffering from 3 or more Tilts, you may spend 1 willpower point to deal aggravated damage with Brawl, Athletics, Weaponry or a Supernatural Merit (if the Merit already costs 1 willpower point, this cost is ignored). Should the opponent be killed, roll your Presence + Expression or Intimidation to strike a badass victory pose. On a Success, you heal a number of lethal or bashing damage equal to your effective Stamina/2 round up. On an Exceptional Success, you heal damage equal to your full effective Stamina. You may only strike a pose once per scene.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 07-13-2016, 10:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T08:17:04-07:00","id":930859,"title":"","content":"I'm thinking about removing Vicious Projectile, and moving the following maneuvers one spot back. The fifth maneuver could be a new spin on Brutality, and Vicious Projectile would become a part of each character's personal arsenal/Supernatural Merits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T08:55:13-07:00","id":930882,"title":"","content":"Fifth dot's initial ability is irrelevant, once someone has their health filled with lethal any damage they take is aggravated anyway.<br /> <br /> How about one that models the famous hooks that send characters flying 10 feet into the air?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T09:04:33-07:00","id":930888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/930832-just-for-fun-mortal-kombat-fighting-style?p=930882#post930882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fifth dot's initial ability is irrelevant, once someone has their health filled with lethal any damage they take is aggravated anyway.<br /> <br /> How about one that models the famous hooks that send characters flying 10 feet into the air?</div> </div> </div> </div> Good point. And that idea for a maneuver is great! I'll make it about knocking opponents into environmental hazards.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T10:33:32-07:00","id":930928,"title":"","content":"The first dot is <i>ridiculously</i> good, by the way; +1 HL, +1 Stamina for the purposes of taking Tilts, and 1/1 Armor <i>that stacks with everything</i> is <i>absurd</i>.<br /> <br /> The second dot is also <i>really</i> good - give someone a -1 to -3 penalty to their Stamina for the purposes of taking Tilts 2/Scene, and your Athletics, Brawl, and Weaponry attacks <i>always</i> deal Lethal damage, no matter what. That latter benefit is <i>stupidly</i> strong, especially for a merit accessible to mortals - you're essentially handing Lethal Brawl attacks (which are normally kind of hard to get) + &quot;nuh-uh, your template ability to reduce damage is dumb and doesn't work&quot;. For reference, that'd normally cost 7xp (for Martial Arts 4 and Kindred Dueling 3, except in this case, the latter applies to <i>all</i> targets, not just vampires).<br /> <br /> The third dot gives you <i>another</i> use of the penalty, +1 HL, and another +1 Stamina for the purposes of Tilts. You reduce all penalties for targeted attacks by 2, to a minimum of -1, and you can spend Willpower to punch someone up to 25 yards away. You know, this would be fine if it didn't give you the non-niche mechanical benefits of Giant as a side note.<br /> <br /> The fourth dot... most people are going to have an Effective Stamina of 0 if you are at all decent at fighting. You're making people <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/444409-milestone-gifts-in-2e\">Fucking Dead</a> in exchange for taking a -1 penalty and hitting them in the arm. You have no limit on usage, and never specify that you have to use the same custom Tilt each time.<br /> <br /> The fifth dot is actually perfectly fine... or would be if you weren't sneaking a +1 HL and +1 effective Stamina for tilts in there.<br /> <br /> What I'd do:<br /> \u2022 Drop the effective Stamina bonus.<br /> \u2022 Reign back the benefits of the second dot a <i>lot</i>.<br /> \u2022 I'd have the fifth dot's first ability only trigger against people with 3+ Tilts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T15:01:15-07:00","id":931033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/930832-just-for-fun-mortal-kombat-fighting-style?p=930928#post930928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The first dot is <i>ridiculously</i> good, by the way; +1 HL, +1 Stamina for the purposes of taking Tilts, and 1/1 Armor <i>that stacks with everything</i> is <i>absurd</i>.<br /> <br /> The second dot is also <i>really</i> good - give someone a -1 to -3 penalty to their Stamina for the purposes of taking Tilts 2/Scene, and your Athletics, Brawl, and Weaponry attacks <i>always</i> deal Lethal damage, no matter what. That latter benefit is <i>stupidly</i> strong, especially for a merit accessible to mortals - you're essentially handing Lethal Brawl attacks (which are normally kind of hard to get) + &quot;nuh-uh, your template ability to reduce damage is dumb and doesn't work&quot;. For reference, that'd normally cost 7xp (for Martial Arts 4 and Kindred Dueling 3, except in this case, the latter applies to <i>all</i> targets, not just vampires).<br /> <br /> The third dot gives you <i>another</i> use of the penalty, +1 HL, and another +1 Stamina for the purposes of Tilts. You reduce all penalties for targeted attacks by 2, to a minimum of -1, and you can spend Willpower to punch someone up to 25 yards away. You know, this would be fine if it didn't give you the non-niche mechanical benefits of Giant as a side note.<br /> <br /> The fourth dot... most people are going to have an Effective Stamina of 0 if you are at all decent at fighting. You're making people <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/444409-milestone-gifts-in-2e\">Fucking Dead</a> in exchange for taking a -1 penalty and hitting them in the arm. You have no limit on usage, and never specify that you have to use the same custom Tilt each time.<br /> <br /> The fifth dot is actually perfectly fine... or would be if you weren't sneaking a +1 HL and +1 effective Stamina for tilts in there.<br /> <br /> What I'd do:<br /> \u2022 Drop the effective Stamina bonus.<br /> \u2022 Reign back the benefits of the second dot a <i>lot</i>.<br /> \u2022 I'd have the fifth dot's first ability only trigger against people with 3+ Tilts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe the whole point of the thread is to make something that simulates how Mortal Kombat mechanics work. Take someone getting stabbed, and he doesn't suffers any significant tilt. See how mere punches spill ridiculous and copious amounts of blood. Etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T15:21:13-07:00","id":931039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/930832-just-for-fun-mortal-kombat-fighting-style?p=931033#post931033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I believe the whole point of the thread is to make something that simulates how Mortal Kombat mechanics work. Take someone getting stabbed, and he doesn't suffers any significant tilt. See how mere punches spill ridiculous and copious amounts of blood. Etc.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah, that's what I was going for, but I didn't get as close as I wanted.<br /> <br /> That being said, the feedback <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1170_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1170\" data-vbnamecard=\"1170\">amechra</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar9102_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"9102\" data-vbnamecard=\"9102\">WHW</a> gave inspired me to re-utilize some ideas for a different Style:<br /> <br /> <b>Ignore The Pain (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b>Strength \u2022\u2022\u2022, Stamina \u2022\u2022\u2022, Brawl \u2022\u2022, Intimidation \u2022\u2022, Iron Stamina \u2022\u2022<br /> <br /> You have trained to be capable of shrugging off damage to your body and can use this fact to intimidate opponents into giving up.<br /> <br /> <b>Tough As Nails (\u2022):</b> You can take a lot more punishment than you ought to. You gain 1/1 Armor, which applies against lethal damage and stacks with Merits and actual Armor. You add 1 dot of effective Stamina to calculate how much damage you must take to receive a Tilt.<br /> <br /> <b>Bone-Breaker (\u2022\u2022):</b> When you make an All-Out Attack, you gain an additional die and reduce the effective Stamina of the opponent by 1 to inflict a Tilt.<br /> <br /> <b>I Don't Think So (\u2022\u2022\u2022):</b> By spending 1 willpower point, you may reflexively roll Presence + Intimidation vs Resolve + Composure. Success reduces the opponent\u2019s Defense OR their next melee attack by your Intimidation dots. Exceptional Success penalizes both.<br /> <br /> <b>Oh, You Didn't (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022):</b> For each Health box filled with bashing or lethal damage beyond your Size, you gain a +1 bonus to Intimidation rolls. Your Intimidation rolls do not suffer penalties from wounds or Tilts.<br /> <br /> <b>That Tickles (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022): </b>If your Health is filled with bashing or lethal, you may spend 1 willpower point to heal 1 point of damage, thus avoiding the roll to remain conscious.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Included Ephsy's comment.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 07-13-2016, 06:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T15:46:30-07:00","id":931049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/930832-just-for-fun-mortal-kombat-fighting-style?p=931039#post931039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <b>That Tickles (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022): </b>if your Health is filled with bashing or lethal, you may spend 1 willpower point to heal 1 point of damage, thus avoiding the roll to remain conscious.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fixed it for you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T17:18:06-07:00","id":931088,"title":"","content":"I Don't Think So gives me a headache. The idea is cool, but after having a heavy crush on opposed rolls that ended up with a violent break up, I can see very jarring problems that don't have anything to do with power:<br /> - How many opponents it targets? One? All of them? Text is unclear.<br /> - Either way, it's another Contested Roll to add into the combat. Nothing slows combat as contested rolls.<br /> <br /> As for the actual style, if I had 5 dots to spend on martial style and had to use it, I would take 2 of it and 3 of Relentless Assault.<br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> Iron Stamina 2 in requirements makes me cry. It turns the Style from 5 dot style into, practically, a 7 dot Style with 2 dots of meh at the start.<br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> As written, you can spam I Don't Think So multiple times - it's a reflexive action (which means it can also be done outside of your turn, btw) that costs Willpower, but doesn't specify that it can be take once per turn (and apparently, Mage Core 2ed claims that you spend one Willpower per action, not per turn, sooooooo, I Don't Think So!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 07-13-2016, 08:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T20:25:04-07:00","id":931163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">As written, you can spam I Don't Think So multiple times - it's a reflexive action (which means it can also be done outside of your turn, btw) that costs Willpower, but doesn't specify that it can be take once per turn <b>(and apparently, Mage Core 2ed claims that you spend one Willpower per action, not per turn, sooooooo, I Don't Think So!)</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Reference please?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T20:59:07-07:00","id":931171,"title":"","content":"Page 213, &quot;Willpower&quot;<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Willpower<br /> A character\u2019s Willpower represents her determination and <br /> her ability to go above and beyond what should be possible to <br /> achieve her goals. Spending a point of Willpower adds a +3 die <br /> bonus to most dice pools, or +2 to a Resistance trait. <b>You can <br /> only spend one point of Willpower per action.</b> </div> </div> </div>Emphasis mine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T04:24:18-07:00","id":931269,"title":"","content":"Sounds like errata material, considering how often turn and action are thrown around interchangeably.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}